UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under IRC Section 894(a) and the U.S.-Japan tax treaty, a permanent establishment is a fixed place of business through which an enterprise carries on its business, establishing the host country''s right to tax attributable business profits. Sakura''s Chicago office with full-time employees negotiating contracts clearly constitutes a PE.
