  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under IRC Section 453(a) and Treas. Reg. Section 15A.453-1(b)(2)(iii), when the mortgage assumed ($350,000) exceeds the seller''s adjusted basis ($250,000), the excess $100,000 is treated as a deemed payment in the year of sale. The contract price and gross profit percentage are computed using this excess, and Year 1 gain on the deemed payment plus first installment totals $168,750.
